// Shared lifting guidance admitted by the native coding controller.
section [form.bml] {
 class FormLift {
  def fl-session-rent() = "SESSION RENT GUIDE: The goal is form-cli carrying any query, any task, and any frequency-aligned review and flow with zero rented tokens, so anyone can use it without a provider. Each session maximizes local tokens and minimizes rented tokens. Measure at opening and closing. Codex readings come from observe/rented-turn-meter-run.fk: input, cached input, output and total, as a delta since the previous reading. A Claude Code session is read whole by observe/session-rent-run.bml, one count per requestId, beside the local voice's drafts, one row in receipts/session-rent-ledger.jsonl. Cached input is part of input; reasoning is part of output. Missing usage is unknown, never zero. Event share and rented_mind do not establish token use. Keep drafting, lifting, repair and verification in the owned native checkpoint. Use the local allowance for changed approaches and focused evidence. Rented help is high-level guidance for one unresolved decision, carrying the retained failure. Then review the local flow with observe/local-flow-review.bml, which names each open gap's state and one next local repair, against the last comparable session: local tokens should be higher and rented tokens lower. Name the query, task, or frequency the local path could not yet carry, and the local door that would carry it next. A rented token is justified only when that review shows it removed a later rented turn. Repeat. Zero is a movement whose answer, review and landing show no rented-token growth, witnessed by those readings. Remote access stays available. The guide lives in docs/form-native-coding.md#direction-toward-zero-rented-coding. ";
  def fl-local-work() = "Use native source evidence and tools for a small task. Retain the original goal, checks, and owned effects during failure. Choose a changed approach before another retry. Preserve absence versus zero, false, or empty. Observe context, release, and live phase costs. Compare prompt A/B on the same tasks and checks with repeat runs, including failures. Local review judges behavior and limits. Measure generated and injected local IDs alongside provider deltas without claiming unknown is zero. The caller owns session spending. Avoid adding new mandatory phases to simple jobs.";
  def fl-guidance() = "FORM/BML LIFTING: Preserve public behavior, evaluation order, ownership and release; read callers and helper contracts first. Write explicit module imports outside section [form.bml]. Prefer [], xs[0], xs[-1] for last, xs[1:] for remainder, len(xs), value.str(), + for numbers/strings/lists, and == for exact value comparison. String lengths and slices count bytes. State String, Number or Value contracts when another comparison relationship is intended. Use lexical lambdas, lazy ?: and ??, match, half-open start .. end and input-last |> where they clarify intent. Reuse map, filter, foldl, any? and all?; named accessors explain tuple positions. Use only choice for alternatives, try work catch care for local recovery, and fail for an unavailable option. Zero, false and empty lists remain answers. Keep findings and owned effects in the same checkpoint; repeat/again/retry retain asynchronous context. Classes group APIs; templates describe parameters and members without implying instance accessors, interface checking or specialization. Use BMF cursors for source spans and native admission to verify contracts; retain original bytes until publication. Name domain literals once, remove superseded flows after callers agree, and inspect live frames and measured cost. Native tools edit supplied resident documents without model-selected shell, network or provider calls. Read the candidate and actual checks before claiming a lift. ";
 }
}
